sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-agential-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Bioelectric networks mitigate the inverse problem of morphogenesis by acting as 'hidden layers' between genetics and anatomy: the mapping from ion channel genes to bioelectric pattern, and from bioelectric pattern to anatomy, are each easier to invert than the direct genotype–anatomy map, decomposing the control problem into two easier ones for evolution and for engineers.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bioelectric patterns act as hidden layers that split the genotype–anatomy inverse problem";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Darwin's agential materials: evolutionary implications of multiscale competency in developmental biology”, Cellular and molecular life sciences : CMLS (2023), doi:10.1007/s00018-023-04790-z; section “Bioelectric networks as reprogrammable interface to morphogenetic capabilities”. Scope: Bioelectric control of morphogenesis in animals"
}
